# BOHEMIA MAIN QUEST -- PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# M03 -- THE RIDGE
#
# HIS BEAT (opening vision, 7/19): "THE BURIAL ON THE RIDGE (tutorial ends here):
# the family climbs a beautiful ridge overlooking Bohemia and buries the sibling
# together. This is ALSO the first full-scope reveal of the whole valley (the BotW
# vista). So the first time you ever see Bohemia's beauty, you see it through
# tears, over a fresh grave. The city's beauty is bound to loss from the first
# frame, and you can never take that view again without the grave in the
# foreground."
#
# AND THE RIDGE IS THE MENU (locked, his): every boot and every return to menu is
# this view, from your sibling's grave, and it UPGRADES per act. So the flag this
# quest sets is not decoration -- it is the title screen's first state, and the far
# end of the bookend he approved on 8/26 ("VERY NICE IDEA TO, LIKE, SWITCH").
#
# THE VERB HERE IS LOOKING, AND THAT IS THE POINT. There is no fight on the ridge
# and nothing to carry away. The tutorial ends with the player standing still.
#
# The cutscene exists (records/BOHEMIA_SCENE_ACT1_RIDGE_BURIAL.json, 15 beats) and
# this re-writes none of it.
#
# draft:true. Every line is an attempt and not one word is approved.

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# The corpus this quest is actually built from. Every id resolves in
# records/BOHEMIA_QUESTBOOK_LAW_INDEX.json and gates/quest_study_gate.js verifies
# the id AND the quoted law title verbatim. A citation is a claim the machine can
# check, never a name-drop.
# @STUDY Q049.W2  PERSISTENT FAMILY META-PROGRESSION (the manor)
#   applied: the ridge is the family's permanent object across a hundred years, the way the manor is: individuals die and the view keeps the record, which is why the flag it sets is the title screen's first state.
# @STUDY Q020.W6  BACKGROUND REACTIVITY (build opens world)
#   applied: the vista is not a cutscene you watch once, it is a place that reads the world back to you differently every act, so the same climb means a different thing in act three.
# @STUDY Q067.X4  FIRST GENERATION IS A BORING SLOG (weak opening
#   applied: the tutorial ends on the biggest view in the game rather than on a chore list, so the first hour closes on the reason to keep playing instead of on an errand.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_m03_the_ridge   The Ridge
@ACT     1
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

@ROLE father   REQ  family=true
@ROLE mother   REQ  family=true

@STAGE 10
  @LOG We carried them up ourselves. Nobody offered and we would have said no.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20
  @LOG Dug it on the ridge, where you can see the whole valley. That was on purpose.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG Stood up there a long time after. First time I have seen all of it at once. It is beautiful and I hate that.
  @DO set_flag act1_ridge_done
  @DO set_flag the_ridge_is_ours
  @DO learn the_whole_valley
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Said something over the grave with everybody standing there. Meant it. Then we all looked at the valley.
  @DO set_flag act1_ridge_done
  @DO set_flag the_ridge_is_ours
  @DO set_flag spoke_at_the_grave
  @DO learn the_whole_valley
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 COMPLETE #risky
  @LOG Walked out to the edge on my own and looked at the city until it got dark. They let me.
  @DO set_flag act1_ridge_done
  @DO set_flag the_ridge_is_ours
  @DO learn the_whole_valley
  @DO complete_objective 20

@OBJ 10  "Carry them up"          target=father
@OBJ 20  "Bury them on the ridge" target=mother

# =====================================================================
# THE CLIMB. The theme is in the first line: the view costs a grave.
# =====================================================================
@TALK climb  speaker=father  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY Up here. All the way up, I know. There is a reason. #tired
  @SAY You have never seen the whole thing at once. Nobody has, not from the street.
  @SAY From up here you see every bit of it. That is what I want them looking at.
  @OPT "Then let's get up there."     [gate: none]  -> dig
  @OPT "Why does it matter what they see?"  [gate: none]  -> why
  @OPT (keep climbing, say nothing)   [gate: none]  SILENCE -> dig
  @NOVERB "Somewhere closer would do"
@END

@TALK why  speaker=father
  @SAY Because in ten years I want to come up here and be able to point. #tired
  @SAY There. And there. We did that. That is what it matters for.
  @OPT (keep climbing)                [gate: none]  SILENCE -> dig
  @OPT "Then we come back up."        [gate: none]  -> dig  @DO learn we_come_back_here
@END

@TALK dig  speaker=father
  @SAY Here. This is the spot. #grief
  @DO set_stage 20
@END

# =====================================================================
# THE GRAVE, AND THE FIRST TIME YOU SEE BOHEMIA. His locked bind: the
# beauty and the loss arrive in the same frame and never come apart.
# =====================================================================
@TALK grave  speaker=mother  entry=stage>=20
  @SAY Look at it. Go on. #grief
  @SAY Ten years I have lived down in that and I did not know it looked like this.
  @SAY Somebody should say something. It does not have to be good.
  @OPT "I'll say it."                 [gate: none]  -> speak
  @OPT "I can't."                     [gate: none]  -> cant
  @OPT (look at the valley, say nothing)  [gate: none]  SILENCE -> look
  @NOVERB "We should have moved years ago"
@END

@TALK speak  speaker=mother
  @SAY Then say it in front of all of us and all of that. #grief
  @OPT (say it)                       [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 31
  @OPT "Not in front of the whole valley."  [gate: none]  -> look
@END

@TALK cant  speaker=mother
  @SAY Nobody is making you. #grief
  @SAY Stand here, then. That is a thing you can do for them too.
  @OPT (stand there)                  [gate: none]  SILENCE -> look
  @OPT "Alright. I'll say it."        [gate: none]  -> speak
@END

@TALK look  speaker=mother
  @SAY It is going to look like this every time you come up here. #grief
  @SAY And they are going to be right there in front of it, every time.
  @OPT (stay with everybody)          [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 30
  @OPT (walk out to the edge alone)   [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 32
@END
